34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The roads closed eleven days, yet the halls kept their evening schedules. That is a gentle reminder that we can plan around the weather.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus data is stark. Two wards lost their links, forcing an hour’s trip. Our hours must adapt to that reality.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The old outreach stops drew forty people, more than our main building! And the evening groups still meet without help. We should trust what already works.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant covers sessions for a year, then the flat budget absorbs them. The vehicle line overran by a third. The funding shape is the trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The register shows retired tradespeople running the repair clinic, but no payroll staff can supervise them. The tool certification lapsed when the technician retired.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, that is wonderful. The evening groups persisting despite the road closures shows real community resilience. We should build on that steady foundation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Rin, that persistence is key. But my data shows remote use peaks after nine, when we lock up. We must extend hours to match that demand.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, wait! If people use the catalogue at night, why do we need a new building? Maybe we just need to keep the lights on longer.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, extending hours sounds simple, but the vehicle line overran by a third. Who pays for the extra fuel and wear?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun is a symptom. The real gap is supervision. No one on payroll can manage the volunteers. We need to fix that first.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, you are right. If the supervision is missing, adding more duties will only cause confusion. We must ensure the helpers are ready before we ask for more.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. But if we extend hours, we need staff to be present. The remote peak suggests we need a different kind of presence, not just more bodies.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, exactly! The evening groups prove people will show up if we just let them. We need to stop building new things and start supporting the old ones that actually work.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, supervision is a staffing issue, but the grant structure is a financial one. Once the year ends, the flat budget absorbs the cost. That is where the trap lies.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the financial trap is real, but it is secondary. If we cannot supervise the existing volunteers, adding new funded duties will just create chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the delivery windows are a worry. If a large client books first, our parts slip. We must choose projects that do not depend on those fragile timelines.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. But my data shows the real gap is after nine. We need to match our presence to when people actually need us, not just when parts arrive.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, I agree. But the digitisation project failed because nobody checked the records. We must avoid repeating that mistake by looking at what already succeeded.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, delivery windows are a symptom. The real issue is that the grant vanishes after twelve months, leaving the flat budget to absorb the shock.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Shizue, delivery windows matter, but they are secondary. If the staff cannot supervise the new duties, late parts just add to the existing chaos.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
