60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am drawn to the Mobile Branch. It brings us to people, avoiding the fragile delivery windows I found.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Mobile Branch directly addresses the lost bus links. It brings the service to the outer wards, solving the access gap I identified.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"The old outreach stops proved people will come to us! The Mobile Branch is basically that, but with a real vehicle. I want to see it work again.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Mobile Branch is a financial trap. My data shows vehicle costs overran by a third. The grant vanishes after a year, leaving the flat budget to bleed.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,The Mobile Branch needs a driver and a supervisor. My data shows no one on payroll is trained to manage that. It is a staffing gap.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle costs are a real worry. But the halls kept their schedules despite the road closures. Perhaps we can plan around the weather, as they did.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle cost is a concern, but the access gap is immediate. If we do not reach those wards, the service fails before it starts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the old stops worked because people showed up! The vehicle cost is scary, but the attendance proves the demand is real.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, attendance proves demand, not sustainability. The grant ends, the vehicle line overruns, and the flat budget absorbs the shock. That is the trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the financial trap is real, but the staffing gap is immediate. If we cannot supervise the driver, the vehicle just sits idle. We must fix the roster first.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, you are right. We must ensure the helpers are ready. I will look at the volunteer register to see if we have the skills to support this new duty.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the staffing gap is real, but the access gap is deeper. If we cannot reach those wards, no amount of supervision helps. We must prioritize the route.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the evening groups prove people self-organize! We don't need a new supervisor; we need to trust the community to keep the lights on.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, supervision is a staffing fix, but the funding structure is a design flaw. Once the grant expires, the flat budget absorbs the vehicle overrun. That is the real trap.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, trust is not a supervision plan. The tool certification lapsed because no one checked. We cannot assume the community will fill the safety gaps.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle worry is valid. But the Digital Archive uses stock tools, avoiding the fragile delivery windows I found. It feels more stable for our timetables.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the Archive is remote, but my data shows the peak demand is after nine. A portal does not solve the physical access gap in the outer wards.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, the old digitisation project failed because nobody finished the job! A portal is just a fancy way to leave half the work undone. I hate that idea.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the Archive avoids the vehicle trap. It uses existing staff and avoids the grant cliff. The funding shape is finally sensible.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the Archive is a relief. It uses existing digital skills, so no new supervision is needed. It avoids the staffing gap I found.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
